def: a way to store files using buckets which consist of objects
use cases:backup/storage,disaster recovery,archive,hybrid cloud storage,application hosting,..
buckets are directories in the clouds where files are the objects
shared global namespace: unique global name across all regions
account regional namespace: use same bucket name across regions
objects have a key this is the full path: composed of prefix+object name
multi-part upload for files bigger than 5GB
tags=unicode key
meta data= additional information given for the object

security policies:
  1) user based:IAM
  2) reource-based:
    2.1) bucket policies:
      2.1.1) json based policies: resources, effect(allow/deny), actions( set of api to allow or deny), principale( what should you do with it)
    2.2) object ACL: based on the file or map
    2.3)  bucket ACL: based on the full bucket
  3) encryption using encryption keys

versioning: doesn't delete previous version just marks it as delete

S3 replication(copying asynchronous,IAM):
  1)CRR/Cross-region replication
  2) SRR/Same-region replication

Storage classes:
  1) standard- generale purpose
  2) standard-infrequent access(IA)
  3) one zone-infrequent access
  4) glacier instant retrieval
  5) glacier flexible retrieval 
  6) glacier deep archive
  7) intelligent tiering 
